>> title: Smash Burger
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: beef, cheese, griddle, burger, lunch
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: cheeseburger, hamburger, diner burger, smashburger, smashed burger, single with cheese, double with cheese
>> pairs-with: homemade-ketchup
>> servings: 2
>> time: 20 min
>> step.1: toast the cut faces in butter 1 min
>> step.2: shape it loose, nothing mixed in
>> step.3: press once hard, season, flip at 2 min, cheese, 1 min
>> step.4: stack two per bun and close

Toast @potato buns{2}(split) cut side down in @unsalted butter{1%Tbs}(14 g) on the griddle ~toast{1%min}, until the faces are gold.

Ball @ground beef{10%oz}(280 g; 80/20 chuck, coarse ground) into four loose 2 1/2-oz balls, handled as little as your hands allow.

Smash @&(~1)beef balls{} onto a #griddle{} filmed with @neutral oil{1%tsp}(5 mL) and screaming hot, season with @kosher salt{1%tsp}(6 g) and @coarse black pepper{1/2%tsp}(1 g), ~sear{2%min} untouched, then flip, lay @American cheese{4%slices} on, and ~sear{1%min}.

Stack @&(~1)patties{} two to a bun on @&(~3)toasted buns{} with @dill pickle chips{8}, @yellow onion{2%Tbs}(shaved paper-thin) and @yellow mustard{2%tsp}(10 mL), and close it.
